-- THE FAIL-CAPABLE HALF of `b1-xmod-default-inherited-tag`.
--
-- A gate made only of the positive fixture cannot fail for the right reason: a
-- method-less impl that silently resolved to NOTHING would also print a value if
-- some other tier happened to answer.  This file is that fixture with EXACTLY ONE
-- dimension flipped -- the interface default is deleted -- and it must stay a LOUD
-- rejection at exit 1, naming the missing method.
--
-- It also bounds the population of `keyForSite`'s `None` arm.  The arm is reached
-- for a cross-module method-less impl whether or not a default exists; what makes
-- the sibling RUN is that a default is there for `emitDefaultRKey` to lift.  With
-- no default there is nothing to route to and the program is rejected before any
-- engine sees it -- so the no-row arm's live population really is the
-- default-inheriting shape and nothing wider.
--
-- HAND-DERIVED: `impl Sz Box` implements no method and `Sz.sz` has no default, so
-- the impl is incomplete.  REJECT on all three verbs.
import iface.{Sz(..), sz}

data Box = Box

impl Sz Box where

main = println (sz Box)
